{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791638693,"nonce":"4diXoN/SHtYXQbe1wW0FL6dRyjc=","message":"Findings 2026-10-10 on the Mac (release, llvm-backend build) for scoping this.\n\nWhat is lowered and what runs: api.lua's module after prune holds 147 program functions (278k HIR text lines); 88% of those lines are its main chunk's segments lua$chunk$0..$11, all called directly by the chunk driver, and only chunk$0 runs (the file returns at line 6 without T); 3 Lua functions are interpreted and none compiled. bitwise and nextvar run about 56 to 63 functions of their lowered set; events about 83. The 67 functions only referenced through funcref are the small $fn adaptors (4,650 lines), so deferring only address-taken targets would save almost nothing: the body has to be lowered at its first call, direct calls included.\n\nWhat first-call lowering needs: every function already has an id and its typed parameter and return types from collect_declarations before any body is lowered, so callers do not need callee bodies. The tiered backend reads deferred bodies through LazyModule::function(id), signature(id) and body_insts(id) only (Scratch::reach, optimize_body, make_interp_body, the lazy compile, OptCache::decode_shells), which a program body source can answer. The hard parts: a late body brings string-literal globals and lifted closures that the installed module and the interpreter must accept (the joining-module path Lua's load uses already adds globals at run time), LoweringContext and the TypedProgram have to outlive lower_program behind a lock (the context holds RefCells but nothing that is not Send), and module-wide facts that read every body (drop_insert facts, purity, error-flag summaries, static-hot detection) need answers for bodies not lowered yet.\n\nSince: HIR values shrank to 80 bytes and the SSA builder no longer goes quadratic on large chunks (0ff7d8d, 22ceae3), which lowers the cost this issue is about without removing it.","files":null}]}